## Bug Description

Uncaught `write EPIPE` error in the Electron main process of Hermes Studio (AppImage). Occurs during the initial "downloading runtime" flow after first launch.

## Stack Trace

```
Error: write EPIPE
at afterWriteDispatched (node:internal/stream_base_commons:159:15)
at writeGeneric (node:internal/stream_base_commons:150:3)
at Socket._writeGeneric (node:net:1025:11)
at Socket._write (node:net:1037:8)
at writeOrBuffer (node:internal/streams/writable:570:12)
at _write (node:internal/streams/writable:499:10)
at Writable.write (node:internal/streams/writable:508:10)
at Socket.<anonymous> (/tmp/.mount_.../resources/app.asar/dist/main/webui-server.js:380:24)
at Socket.emit (node:events:509:28)
at addChunk (node:internal/streams/readable:563:12)
```

## Root Cause

In `dist/main/webui-server.js:378-385`, `startWebUiServer()` spawns the Web UI server child process with `stdio: [\"ignore\", \"pipe\", \"pipe\"]` and pipes its stdout/stderr to the parent processes stdout/stderr via `process.stdout.write()` and `process.stderr.write()`. Neither call has an error handler, so when the parent pipe is closed (e.g. terminal closes, launch script exits), the write throws an unhandled **EPIPE** exception that crashes the main process.

```javascript
// Lines 378-385 — NO error handling
serverProc.stdout?.on("data", (chunk) => {
    bridgeStartup.observe(chunk);
    process.stdout.write(`[webui] ${chunk}`);  // EPIPE here
});
serverProc.stderr?.on("data", (chunk) => {
    bridgeStartup.observe(chunk);
    process.stderr.write(`[webui] ${chunk}`);  // EPIPE here too
});
```

## Suggested Fix

Three lines of protection: try/catch around writes + silent error handlers on both streams:

```javascript
serverProc.stdout?.on("data", (chunk) => {
    bridgeStartup.observe(chunk);
    try {
        process.stdout.write(`[webui] ${chunk}`);
    } catch {
        /* EPIPE: parent stdout closed */
    }
});
serverProc.stdout?.on("error", () => { /* EPIPE: ignore */ });

serverProc.stderr?.on("data", (chunk) => {
    bridgeStartup.observe(chunk);
    try {
        process.stderr.write(`[webui] ${chunk}`);
    } catch {
        /* EPIPE: parent stderr closed */
    }
});
serverProc.stderr?.on("error", () => { /* EPIPE: ignore */ });
```

## Environment

- Hermes Studio 0.6.23 (AppImage)
- Arch Linux, Wayland
- App launched with `--no-sandbox`

## Additional Context

The error is non-fatal to the runtime download itself — the runtime may download correctly before the EPIPE occurs, but the uncaught exception dialog confuses users. The fix is in the `startWebUiServer()` function within the webui-server module.

